 "notes": "The three scuttled wrecks off Xatt l-Aħmar: MV Xlendi (80 x 12 m, upside down, 42 m shore side, 44 m sea side), MV Karwela (43 m, upright, deck 30 m, bow 39 m) and MV Cominoland (34.5 m, upright, 35–42 m), with the car wreck. Bearings from the ladders (130°, 160°, 200°), spacing (about 50 m and 60 m), depth lines and the drop-off 25 m out, checked against the maltadives.com GPS positions and the OSM MV Xlendi node; shoreline from OpenStreetMap. Contours are drawn as straight lines parallel to the shore and all positions are approximate; the Hephaestus (2022) is not shown.",
